From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: unwind KMS initialization and drain snapshot producers

Make each KMS backend undo its completed initialization steps and reserve
full teardown for a successfully initialized KMS. Preserve the existing
Uke VRR getter and the Linux 7.3 component/DRM interfaces. Clear released
hardware pointers and clean up DPU self-refresh helpers before VM release.

Serialize the bounded display fault callback with handler withdrawal.
Cancel pending commit hrtimers and drain their workers while IRQs and
mapped display resources remain available. Withdraw the snapshot worker
under its queue lock and drain outside that lock, so late queue attempts
cannot use a destroyed worker. Preserve GPU callback dispatch behavior.
Reset IRQ ownership after freeing it, including post-install failures.

The initialization/unwind changes adapt Dmitry Baryshkov's GPL-2.0-only v3
series, patches 1-14:
https://patchew.org/linux/20261024-msm-kms-destroy-fixes-v3-0-66a30120a5ea@oss.qualcomm.com/
Additional producer synchronization follows the actual Linux 7.3 callers
and the hrtimer_cancel API. No board timing or address is transferred.
This does not establish physical acceptance or historical fault causation.

Upstream-Status: Pending [Linux 7.3 adaptation and producer lifetime fixes]
Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
